44
00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:39.450
My solution was really based off of two hypotheses.

45
00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:44.450
First of all, the sample letter that they were sent to patients was really confusing in general.

46
00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:52.450
The language itself didn't feel really concise and clear.

47
00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:58.450
Also, the reader, because of that language, wasn't interpreting it in the right way.

48
00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:02.450
These are all hypotheses that I have.

49
00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:09.450
Based off that sample letter, I wanted to identify some things that they needed,

50
00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:15.450
where it stood, what to action next, who to speak with.

51
00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:23.450
I also wanted to add some sort of guide for people that didn't require a sign-in,

52
00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:26.450
